{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_6c512f6c94e14bf7939ee8a362cc21b6597c9b0a21d07b62cc04e3c88651d819"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: provider-specific logic must stay in registries and per-layer tables rather than branching on provider names, with a drift test (TestProviderKnowledgeStaysInRegistry) enforcing this boundary."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d951608442a7fa4b659a80ca9180397e52a05031934f3677b0430157672d26a7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md gives coding-agent guidelines—state assumptions before implementing, keep changes minimal and surgical, and turn tasks into verifiable, test-driven goals."}],"claim_ids":["clm_6c512f6c94e14bf7939ee8a362cc21b6597c9b0a21d07b62cc04e3c88651d819","clm_d951608442a7fa4b659a80ca9180397e52a05031934f3677b0430157672d26a7"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_f3455910a9154937bb0f320095705ae6","id":"pg_addd55b4bf77547887a3bc5bfde94985","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/podiom-podiom-agents-md-78025f740077-bc5bfde94985.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_75058655547d568fb08a12e8d517bfab"],"title":"Podiom/Podiom/AGENTS.md @ 78025f740077","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f3455910a9154937bb0f320095705ae6"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0464bd7c1caae66a132c5829bca2041f41dd5249ed25e236212e939ee8b18f60"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Goals run deliberately autonomously: the lead agent and linked tasks or schedules run with full access and no per-action approval prompts, while tool activity is recorded on the goal timeline."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4fdf498203856b650c8e8c6c71458f9585a556b079b559c5b904387b1cf8196c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The layout includes a thin CLI client (cmd/podiom), a daemon combining web server, scheduler, and core (cmd/podiomd), internal packages, and a Svelte/Vite/TypeScript/Tailwind web UI built into podiomd."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5e8e3a9635acf947cdc2955879fa04f99cb272a4b432ede53b7e636e4efa1d5c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Podiom stores a canonical history for every session and can replay that history onto a fresh backing CLI session when the provider or profile changes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_66d8978da7faff08f30f285bd52810e420214e5d3982b88a2cf7b8d7e74aec09"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The web UI defaults to 127.0.0.1:8787, with bind address and port configurable via server.bind and server.port in config.yaml; a browser-native WebSocket endpoint at /api/ws is also documented."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8040fb01daba8a75b63cd13f5668dd58ccb3ab9b1192368a0c4adbe336e8d767"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project targets developers already using Claude Code or OpenAI Codex locally who want persistent, reviewable agent work, recurring jobs, project context, and an audit trail in one workspace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a93c12d1c4874d76db8dd80f5a75b5ca0fb7015820cb0ceee237d2f625173ee7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The podiomd daemon embeds the web SPA and uses pure-Go SQLite, so it needs no external web assets or cgo at runtime."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c08851172ef66a32e702defd2c6498a685fa13b306492abbd9b6f965034fc58a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Native iOS and Android mobile apps can connect to standalone daemons or an opt-in, API-only Home Assistant LAN endpoint, and the same core can run as a Home Assistant add-on or in a container."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c7978f1f3f7cee387ead86ac6a5fc25a82c330faea9d2540c15615fc2ecab7fc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Podiom is local-first: all runtime state lives under one overridable root ($PODIOM_HOME, defaulting to ~/.podiom/), and provider CLIs keep their native authentication and policy controls."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ddf17bd31007bce13bf48a694c7530e45d25b953694cec5b3261ded43d03c321"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository points to docs/requirements/foundation.md as the authoritative foundation specification, at version v1.6."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fb975e63c4deff15c7cbd8230e1d99226cd9ed3b8423ea3a2c574c84df73bd52"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Podiom does not replace the provider runtime; it shells out to the native claude and codex CLIs and reuses their models, MCP servers, tools, skills, and authentication."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fbd6e12dc15f991c4eadb946711ba4e393557d97a47701d38f23e4d0c5d1eeb8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A goal gives one lead agent an outcome to own over days or weeks; the agent turns it into roadmap tasks and schedules, delegates work, and records periodic reviews with progress, evidence, and next steps."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0464bd7c1caae66a132c5829bca2041f41dd5249ed25e236212e939ee8b18f60","clm_4fdf498203856b650c8e8c6c71458f9585a556b079b559c5b904387b1cf8196c","clm_5e8e3a9635acf947cdc2955879fa04f99cb272a4b432ede53b7e636e4efa1d5c","clm_66d8978da7faff08f30f285bd52810e420214e5d3982b88a2cf7b8d7e74aec09","clm_8040fb01daba8a75b63cd13f5668dd58ccb3ab9b1192368a0c4adbe336e8d767","clm_a93c12d1c4874d76db8dd80f5a75b5ca0fb7015820cb0ceee237d2f625173ee7","clm_c08851172ef66a32e702defd2c6498a685fa13b306492abbd9b6f965034fc58a","clm_c7978f1f3f7cee387ead86ac6a5fc25a82c330faea9d2540c15615fc2ecab7fc","clm_ddf17bd31007bce13bf48a694c7530e45d25b953694cec5b3261ded43d03c321","clm_fb975e63c4deff15c7cbd8230e1d99226cd9ed3b8423ea3a2c574c84df73bd52","clm_fbd6e12dc15f991c4eadb946711ba4e393557d97a47701d38f23e4d0c5d1eeb8"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_f3455910a9154937bb0f320095705ae6","id":"pg_d0ccd95f6cc2529baf828934566db70f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/podiom-podiom-readme-md-78025f740077-8934566db70f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_bddcfe8e41e758169cb1ca925f75f8b9"],"title":"Podiom/Podiom/README.md @ 78025f740077","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:31:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f3455910a9154937bb0f320095705ae6"}
